ndirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"degeneracy d.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","title":"MaximalCliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","title":"Cliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/Element":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/Element","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/element","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Element","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"MaximalCliques.Element"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Vertex":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[],"title":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\